Furthermore, since $\ensuremath{\text{\rm int}\,}\ensuremath{\text{\rm dom}\,} f\subset\ensuremath{\text{\rm int}\,}\ensuremath{\text{\rm dom}\,} h$ 
and $L(\ensuremath{\text{\rm int}\,}\ensuremath{\text{\rm dom}\,} f)\subset\ensuremath{\text{\rm int}\,}\ensuremath{\text{\rm dom}\,} j$, we obtain
$x\in\ensuremath{\text{\rm int\,dom}\,} h$ and $Lx\in\ensuremath{\text{\rm int\,dom}\,} j$. Thus, there exists 
